# Pluggable module architecture (non-negotiable)

The backend is a modular monolith of self-contained, pluggable modules:

- Modules live in `backend/app/modules/<name>/` and expose one entry point: a
  `module` object (`ModuleSpec`) in `module.py` with `name`, `version`, `router`,
  optional `soft_deps`, and `setup`/`shutdown` hooks.
- **A module may import ONLY from `app.core.*` and its own package — never from
  `app.modules.<other>`.** Cross-module interaction goes through:
  - `app.core.registry` — capabilities published/consumed by string name, resolved
    at runtime, absence handled gracefully; or
  - `app.core.events` — publish/subscribe on named events.
- `soft_deps` are advisory: a module degrades gracefully (feature off + warning)
  when a dependency is disabled. Never crash at import or startup.
- Modules are toggled via config (`TS_ENABLED_MODULES`); the app boots with any subset.
- Shared contracts (Pydantic models/enums) live in `app/core/contracts/` only.
- Each module owns its DB tables, migrations, and tests. Reference other modules'
  data by ID + events, not foreign keys into their tables.

# Product invariants (from docs/TenderShield_Full_Build_Doc.md)

- Numbers never come from the LLM — BOQ math, date math, severity are deterministic code.
- Every extracted fact carries `source_page` + verbatim `source_quote` and passes
  quote verification.
- Artifact validators: no invented quotes, no uncited clauses, no invented numbers.
- Org isolation (RLS) on every org-scoped table.
- Billing truth = verified webhooks only; client redirects activate nothing.
- Tender/OCR text is untrusted input (prompt-injection defense).
- Money in minor units (paise), never float.
